SUMMARY:You Might Like This @ RADIUS\, Delft
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
DTSTART:20261112T190000Z
DTEND:20261112T203000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join us for You Might Like This @ RADIUS in Delft\, where six a
 rtists\, researchers\, and makers will share their explorations of and enc
 ounters with social media and algorithmic systems. We’re celebrating our
  10th anniversary this fall by reflecting on the algorithmic feed\, which
  is turning 10 as well. This event explores how how algorithms shape our o
 nline environments. \nFor this event\, we’re setting up shop in Delft\,
  a city we haven’t visited before\, but one with a strong connection to
  algorithmic systems thanks to Delft University of Technology. We’re ver
 y excited to have Seda Gürses as our guest programmer. Seda is Associate
  Professor in the Department of Multi-Actor Systems at TU Delft. Her resea
 rch focuses on privacy engineering\, protective optimisation technologies\
 , software engineering and the political economy of computational infrastr
 uctures. She is examining how technical systems intersect with social just
 ice and governance.  \nStay posted further down on this page for more inf
 ormation on speakers and the programme. \nWhat you need to know\n🗓 Date
 : Thursday 12 November 2025\n📍 Location: RADIUS\, Kalverbos 20\, 2611 X
 W Delft\n⏰ Time: Program starts at 20:00 CET\, doors open at 19:30 CET\n
 🎟 Tickets: on-site €8\,- / on-site student discount €5\,- / online
  livestream €5 \n♿️ Accessibility note\nDue to the historic nature o
 f the building the Water Tower is unfortunately non accessible for persons
  with disabilities. \n🩵 This programme is kindly supported by the Crea
 tive Industries Fund NL and Het Cultuurfonds.
URL:https://thehmm.nl/event/you-might-like-this-radius-delft/
CATEGORIES:The Hmm
END:VEVENT
