SUMMARY:The Hmm TO the Chinese Internet
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
DTSTART:20261125T190000Z
DTEND:20261125T203000Z
DESCRIPTION:What does the Chinese internet look like from the inside?\n‎\
 n\nThe Hmm’s Chinese Internet Tour takes you on a guided trip through Ch
 ina’s social media ecosystem\, led by media anthropologist Dino Ge Zhang
  whose research focuses on emotions and aesthetics on the Sinophone intern
 et. \nWe’ll visit destinations like the face-filter app Meitu (美图公
 司) and the Myspace-like relic Qzone (QQ空间) to the TikTok-style short
 -video platform Kuaishou (快手)\, where artists\, researchers\, and desi
 gners with local expertise show us how these platforms work\, what makes t
 hem distinct\, and how to navigate the practical barriers to using them. \
 n\n‎\nWe often think of the social media platforms we use in the West as
  global. Yet behind China’s Great Firewall\, a vast and largely separate
  social media ecosystem has developed\, with platforms that are used by hu
 ndreds of millions of people but remain relatively unfamiliar outside the
  country. These platforms have their own cultures and conventions\, shaped
  by China’s particular internet landscape. They are also spaces where ne
 w trends\, memes\, and visual languages emerge\, many of which eventually
  make their way onto the global internet\, sometimes months or years later
 .\n‎\nFor people outside China\, getting a glimpse of these platforms me
 ans seeing the internet from a perspective that is rarely available. Many
  got their first glimpse of this world in January 2025\, when RedNote (小
 红书) surged in popularity after the US government threatened to ban Tik
 Tok. For a brief moment\, the platform became a possible refuge for TikTok
  users\, attracting a wave of curious newcomers from outside China. But Ti
 kTok was only unavailable for about a day\, and most of these new users re
 mained RedNote day-trippers.\n‎\nThe Hmm’s Chinese Internet Tour picks
  up where that moment left off. Moving beyond RedNote\, we’ll explore th
 e wider landscape of platforms\, communities\, aesthetics\, and strange di
 gital corners that make up China’s internet\, and get a sense of what it
  looks like from the inside.\n‎\nWhat you need to know\n‎ Guided by Di
 no Zhang\n\n\n📅 Date: Wednesday 25 November 2026\n🕗 Times: 20.00 –
  21.30 CET\n📍 Location: The Inbetween\n🎟 Tickets: €5\n‎\n\n‎
 💚 This programme is kindly supported by the Creative Industry Fund.
URL:https://thehmm.nl/event/the-hmm-to-the-chinese-internet/
CATEGORIES:The Hmm
END:VEVENT
