X-PRUTS-UUID:thehmm:10146-1797015600-1797037200@thehmm.nl
X-PRUTS-RADAR-ID:thehmm:10146-1797015600-1797037200@thehmm.nl
X-PRUTS-OCCURRENCE-ID:thehmm:10146-1797015600-1797037200@thehmm.nl:2026-12-
 11T19:00:00+01:00
DTSTAMP:20261028T031317Z
SUMMARY:Celebrating 10 Years of The Hmm + Book Launch
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
DTSTART:20261211T180000Z
DTEND:20261212T000000Z
DESCRIPTION:Earlier this year\, the internet was briefly filled with the ho
 pe that 2026 might become the new 2016. In quasi-historical fashion\, user
 s resurfaced early Instagram filters and interfaces\, Tumblr-motivational
  quotes\, old memes\, and other fragments of a supposedly simpler internet
 . Collectively\, it became a meditation on how social media used to be bet
 ter\, or at least how much it felt better. Though users relied on a more g
 eneralised nostalgia to resurrect the aesthetic of the time\, they were\,
  in a sense\, correct. The internet really did feel different. 2016 was th
 e year that all news feeds became algorithmic\, and with it our relationsh
 ip with social media fundamentally changed.\n‎\n\nSerendipitously\, The
  Hmm was also born ten years ago\, in 2016. Since then\, we have tried to
  trace\, interrogate and intervene in the forces shaping our online lives\
 , including the algorithmic feed itself. To celebrate this legacy\, we are
  throwing a festive evening at W139 in Amsterdam\, filled with performance
 s\, workshops\, drinks and more.\n‎\n‎Suggested For You: Reflecting on
  a decade in the feed\nThe evening will also mark the launch of our 10-yea
 r anniversary publication: Suggested For You: Reflecting on a Decade in th
 e Feed. Part celebration\, part reflection\, the book looks back at the al
 gorithmic feed and the decade of internet cultures that has unfolded aroun
 d it. Featuring essays\, interviews\, image contributions and artist profi
 les from Ruba Al-Sweel\, Evelyn Austin and Rejo Zenger\, Jak Ritger\, Soyu
 n Park and Leo Scarin\, Noura Tafeche\, Neema Githere\, Alex Quicho\, Cons
 tant Dullaart\, Mamali Shafahi and Ali Eslami\, Danielle Brathwaite-Shirle
 y\, K Allado McDowell and Aidan Walker\, the publication brings together a
  range of perspectives on how the algorithmic feed has come to shape life
  online.\nYou can already pre-order the book. It will be available to pick
 -up and purchase at the event.\n‎\nProgram\nSpeakers\, workshops and per
 formances to be announced soon.\n‎\nWhat you need to know\n\n📅 Date:
  Friday 11 December 2026\n🕗 Times: 19.00 – 1.00 CET\n📍 Location: W
 139\, Warmoesstraat 139\, 1012 JB Amsterdam & Bar San Francisco\, Zeedijk
  40\, 1012 AZ Amsterdam\n🎟 Tickets: Free\, but please register!\n‎\n\
 n‎💚 This programme is kindly supported by the Amsterdams Fonds voor d
 e Kunsten and Het Cultuurfonds. Suggested For You is supported by Mondriaa
 nfonds.
URL:https://thehmm.nl/event/celebrating-10-years-of-the-hmm-book-launch/
CATEGORIES:The Hmm
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
